Statcom Expert & Project Management
Who we are
Elia Grid International (EGI) is a global engineering consultancy company, part of Elia Group (Belgium) and 50Hertz (Germany), specialising in complex power system challenges. Our goal is to provide high-quality solutions for the challenges of the energy transition. Our multidisciplinary team of experts offer strategic, technical, and regulatory advice in all fields related to power transmission, as well as a range of specialist solutions to a diverse and international client base in the power sector.
Elia Grid International has offices in Belgium, Germany, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (KSA), and Malaysia.
Your function
EGI wishes to reinforce its team working on Owner's Engineering in the context of deep integration of renewable energy sources, Energy and Balancing Market Integration. To achieve this, we are looking for Statcom Expert & Project Managers to be responsible for delivering expertise in all aspects of HVDC projects (with a focus on converter stations).
With your extensive experience in HV Reactive Power Compensation System technology and proven track record in project management, you will take responsibility for the preparation, planning and implementation of EGI Statcom projects. Your responsibilities will include the quality, budget, schedule and reporting of your project and/or sub-project. In addition to your specialist experience, you must also be an efficient organizer, assertive, a capable communicator and a team player.
 Typical Activities Involve (but Are Not Limited To)
 Defining plant-specific requirements for the Statcom system especially defining single line diagrams and Statcom layouts included in client substations;
 Editing technical guidelines for Statcom components and equipment and their interface connection;
 Supervision and quality checks during the Statcom plant and its auxiliary system installation process;
 Controlling the entire technical implementation process from developing concepts, and drafting tender documents to award contracts and accepting delivery from customers and contracting parties;
 Ensuring that technical customer requirements are implemented and compliance with the relevant guidelines and regulations in accordance with all safety regulations;
 Drawing up comparisons of technical and economic alternatives and doing preparatory work for cost-intensive investment decisions;
 Actively collaborating with project managers, drawing up reports, budget forecasts and schedules, attending construction meetings, placing orders under framework agreements;
 Quality control by taking part in factory acceptance tests and on-site operational tests Statcom plant primary equipment;
 Approval and checking of Statcom equipment and plant documentation;
 Determine basic requirements for Statcom components and equipment, transformer and busbar control and protection equipment and Statcom auxiliary power supply concepts.
 Your profile
 Master's degree in electrical engineering;
 5+ years of relevant experience with Statcom, Reactive Power Compensation systems (SVC, MSCDN, etc…) and primary and secondary equipment for HV substations (up to 400kV);
 Experiences (basics) in electrical network calculation, insulation coordination and Statcom design studies;
 Knowledge in HV/MV transformer and cable design, control cables and optical fibre cables;
 Knowledge of modelling languages, data analytics and simulation software widely used in the energy industry (PowerFactory, PSSE, Matlab, etc);
 Great knowledge and experience in the use of ITWO, SAP and MS Office;
 Fluent in English and German;
 Knowledge of French and/or another language is a strong asset.
 What we offer
 Permanent contract or freelance position;
 Attractive salary package and an extensive array of fringe benefits;
 Exciting, professional and international environment in a fast-growing company;
 Unique training, personal development and growth opportunities;
 At EGI, we value diversity and inclusion. We are firmly committed to promoting gender equality in all aspects of our organization, from recruitment to professional development. We believe that diverse teams are more creative, innovative, and high-performing. Join us to contribute to an environment where everyone has equal opportunities for growth and fulfilment.
Choose EGI and help us guide the worldwide power sector into a future of clean and sustainable energy, smarter and more flexible grids, decentralized production and HVDC systems that span across seas and land to interconnect countries, regions, and different energy markets for the benefit of generations to come.
Location
Berlin – Mobility required: 30% worldwide (willingness to travel abroad for international assignments depending on the business development or project needs).
Want to know more about us?
Check our website and our LinkedIn page for last news and updates.

With just over 10 years of experience in the Portuguese market, we share our DNA with more than 200 workers and position our offer according to 3 lines of service:
 Strategy (Outsourcing, NeXel, Team as a Service, Tech Academies);
 R&D (Bootcamps, POC, Tech Lab);
 Nearshore.
 In ADENTIS, we focus on PEOPLE. This is our emotional salary:
 Great Work-Life balance;
 Very flexible organizational routine;
 Health benefits (for you and your family);
 Team Building activities;
 Over 300 protocols to offer you great discounts in different areas;
 Continuous professional development sponsored by our Training and Certification Department;
 Regular feedback on your performance through a personalized plan;
 Comprehensive career plan and progression involving assertive performance reviews.
 Role Overview: Responsible for defining core product evolutions, building roadmaps, and managing the backlog for Dealer Management Solutions (DMS) across Europe (focusing on regions using iCar, Datacar, and Eris). 
 Key Responsibilities: 
 Define goals and manage product roadmaps in collaboration with the DMS Product Director. 
 Monitor user experience, legal requirements, and conduct market/competitor/customer context analysis. 
 Validate requirements (Epics and Features), acceptance criteria, and manage the product backlog and sprint priorities. 
 Oversee delivery approval, pilot phases, and collaborate with deployment teams. 
 Participate in pre-sales presentations, quotations, and customer/supplier meetings. 
 Manage team activities (performance objectives, training, competencies, and recruitment needs). 
 Tech Stack & Core Requirements: 
 Domain Expertise: Strong knowledge of the automotive business and substantial experience with a DMS (Dealer Management Solutions) solution. 
 Methodologies & Frameworks: SDLC (Software Development Life Cycle) process, Agile/Scrum backlog management (Epics, Features, Sprints). 
 Soft Skills: Strong written and verbal communication skills in English , cross-collaboration capabilities across international R&D and operations teams, and stakeholder management. 
 If you want to be part of a real People First organization, apply now!
 We walk with you!
 At Adentis we defend equality and value diversity. We create a safe, diverse environment where opportunities are equal for all employees! 
 We do not discriminate based on age, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender, disability or any factor other than merit. 
 All candidates with skills for the position are welcome!

A Company you will be happy to grow with! 
 At InnoTech, it´s all about connecting people with business through technology. We truly care about you, your happiness , and your well-being . We look for passionate people who are eager to learn , evolve , and grow with us - because growth is in our DNA. This commitment has been consistently recognized: we are proud to be a Great Place to Work for five consecutive years, to be one of the Best IT Companies in Portugal , and to be recognized as a Best Workplace Wellbeing . We are also proud to hold ISO 27001 and ISO 9001 certifications , reinforcing our commitment to information security, quality , and continuous improvement . For us, sustainability is not just a buzzword. Integrity, social responsibility , and people-first values guide everything we do. Join our team of 180+ InnoTechers and bring your talent as a Senior Product Owner – Research & Ontology .
 Your Mission Will Be 
 Define and drive product roadmaps for AI research, semantic search, ontology development, metadata management, and AI-powered product capabilities, ensuring alignment with business strategy and customer needs;
 Translate research findings, technical concepts, and business objectives into clear product requirements, user stories, acceptance criteria, and prioritized backlogs;
 Collaborate with Product Management, Research, Engineering, Architecture, Data, and UX teams to turn experimental AI initiatives into scalable, customer-focused solutions;
 Manage cross-team dependencies, delivery priorities, risks, and ownership transitions, ensuring effective coordination and continuous value delivery across the product lifecycle;
 Support customer discovery and stakeholder alignment while mentoring other Product Owners and promoting best practices in product management.
 You Will Need 
 At least 3–5 years of experience as a Product Owner , with a strong understanding of Agile methodologies, backlog management, prioritization techniques, and cloud-based software delivery;
 Solid technical knowledge of modern software architectures, including distributed systems, APIs, microservices, and the integration of AI and data capabilities into complex product ecosystems ;
 Experience with semantic search , information retrieval , metadata management, knowledge discovery, ontologies, taxonomies, or related information architecture concepts ;
 Strong stakeholder management, communication, problem-solving, and cross-functional collaboration skills, with the ability to balance business value, technical feasibility, risks, and dependencies;
 CPLP nationality or an EU work permit is required to facilitate employment.
 Would Be Awesome If You Have 
 BSc or MSc in Computer Science/Engineering, Information Technology, or related fields;
 Hands-on product experience with Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), vector databases, Large Language Models (LLMs), semantic technologies, or AI-powered user experiences;
 Familiarity with AI evaluation, governance, privacy, security, explainability, and regulatory requirements for AI-enabled products;
 Experience transitioning research, experimentation, and prototypes into production-ready capabilities, working closely with Research, Data, Platform, and Engineering teams;
 Experience with Jira, Confluence, or similar collaboration tools, alongside an interest in coaching and developing other Product Owners.
 What We Offer 
 Health-focused partnerships, including free mental health support;
 25 days of vacation, including your birthday, Carnival, and a bridging day between Christmas and New Year;
 Half a vacation day on your children's birthday and a school supplies voucher;
 Petsitting partnerships and a pet bereavement day;
 Regular team buildings, four annual company parties, game nights, and social events;
 InnoSports initiatives (football, marathons, and more);
 Events focused on sustainability and social responsibility actions.
 Are you convinced? Come see it for yourself. 
 Join our Top-Notch Team!

